A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F8238b0bd-1624-4cbd-8a34-fc44254ec8eb_1080x1080.jpeg 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\" loading=\"lazy\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"icon-noB79L\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><h4><strong>Free Online Intro Session</strong></h4><p>Register your interest here to join our free online introductory session to learn about the framework that we will be sharing during the program.</p><p class=\"button-wrapper\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://beingme.com.sg/power-and-pause&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Intro Session Details&quot;,&quot;action&quot;:null,&quot;class&quot;:&quot;button-wrapper&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"ButtonCreateButton\"><a class=\"button primary button-wrapper\" href=\"https://beingme.com.sg/power-and-pause\"><span>Intro Session Details</span></a></p><div><hr></div><p></p>",
  "body_text": "It’s 2026. How often are we still celebrating exhaustion as a badge of honour, or mistaking constant busyness for true effort? \n\nWe push, strive, overextend, and tell ourselves we are simply being committed. \n\nAnd the parami of viriya invites us into a wiser relationship with energy.\n\nViriya is often translated as energy or effort, but it carries the spirit of courage — the courage to keep showing up, especially when life feels difficult. \n\nThis doesn’t mean we force ourselves into exhaustion. And we certainly don’t have to swing to the other extreme of giving up, checking out, or “lying flat” — 躺平 (tǎng píng), as the trending Chinese phrase goes. \n\nWe want to find the middle way between overexertion and passivity. \n\nLike tuning a string instrument, the effort cannot be too tight or too loose. It needs the right tension for harmony and balance to arise.\n\nInvestigating their relationship with viriya, the practitioner asks:\n\nWhat is worth giving my energy to? What drains me unnecessarily? What supports clarity and well-being?\n\nThis is especially important in meditation. \n\nWe show up for practice because it is well worth the effort. \n\nEach time the mind wanders, we begin again. Not harshly, not lazily, but steadily. \n\nOver time, this sustained effort becomes a quiet strength.\n\nAwakening, healing, and growth rarely happen through one dramatic breakthrough. \n\nMore often than not, they are the fruit of choosing to show up, one breath, one step, one day at a time. \n\n---\n\nMeditation Practice:\n\nOver 6-7 June 2026, the TAP community cultivated the parami of viriya with a mindfulness practice of awareness of breath. We closed the session with reading a poem by Ullie-Kaye.\n\nTap Play to Practice Together:\n\nThis post is free for 4 weeks, and then archived for paid subscribers to support a sustainable, long-term sharing of mindful content. Upgrade to receive lifetime access to the full archive and ongoing updates.\n\nShare\n\n---\n\nThe Wholehearted Woman Retreat\n\nA five-day mindfulness retreat into quiet wisdom and the light within\n\n1-5 October 2026\nSiem Reap, Cambodia\n\nLed by Erin Lee\n\nJoin Erin at Angkor Wat\n\n---\n\nPower & Pause Retreat\n\nA high-touch program supported by structured processes, guided practices, and reflective assignments\n\n24 - 28 September 2026\nUbud, Bali\n\nLed by Subba Sattvic and Erin Lee\n\nFree Online Intro Session\n\nRegister your interest here to join our free online introductory session to learn about the framework that we will be sharing during the program.\n\nIntro Session Details\n\n---",
